{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGD9P5FVZCED1YHPFAX29DM","title":"Keep the root README as a product entry point","decision":"Keep reader-facing positioning, proof, quickstart, limits, and documentation links in the root README. Enforce exhaustive storage, MCP, and command contracts in crate-specific documentation instead of requiring internal identifiers in the repository landing page.","alternatives":[{"option":"Keep all public contract tokens in README.md","why_rejected":"This produced a 922-line landing page that hides the product difference and duplicates reference documentation."}],"forcing":"The root README is the first public product surface, while crate READMEs already own the detailed contracts.","scope":["README.md","scripts/check-doc-release-refs.sh"],"commits":["15fc455cb3eeceeecdb6a3b6e9e17c9eb31495fa"],"author":"codex","confidence":"high","tags":[],"ts":1784035989679}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGDCD7HTDAQ4W9690TVVW4G","title":"Run the flagship demo through projection trust APIs","decision":"Expose read-only projection helpers for authority recall and self-inspection, then use those same core paths in the dependency-free CLI demo. This makes the demo prove the real trust policy without requiring SurrealDB.","alternatives":[{"option":"Recreate trust verdicts in demo-only CLI code","why_rejected":"That would be a marketing simulation able to drift from the engine policy."},{"option":"Require Docker for the flagship demo","why_rejected":"That would break the zero-setup first-run promise and reduce the chance that a repository visitor sees the differentiator."}],"forcing":"The installed demo must prove self-inspection and result trust with no services while using production logic.","scope":["crates/nahuali-core/src/**","crates/nahuali-cli/src/commands/demo.rs"],"commits":["15fc455cb3eeceeecdb6a3b6e9e17c9eb31495fa"],"author":"codex","confidence":"high","tags":[],"ts":1784036078833}

